<p>when $p = 1$, we get taxicab norm, $p=2$, we get Euclidean norm and if $p$ approaches $\infty$, we will get the infinity norm or maximum norm:</p>

<p>$$
|\pmb x|_{\infty}:=\max_i|x_i|.
$$</p>

<p>The p-norm is related to the generalized mean or power mean.</p>

<p>when $0&lt;p&lt;1$ (wiki)</p>

<h3 id="maximum-norm-special-case-of--infinity-norm--uniform-norm-or-supremum-norm">Maximum norm (special case of : infinity norm , uniform norm or supremum norm)</h3>

<p>$$
|x|_{\infty} :=max(|x_1|, …, |x+|)
$$</p>

